  "body": "## What changed\n\n`assets/posts/sinumerik.cps` wrote the engine's generic work-offset word verbatim, so a setup on offset 5 or 6 opened each section with `G58` / `G59`. On the 840D those are axial programmable offsets, not settable frames (Siemens 840D sl Fundamentals: settable zero offsets `G54`..`G57`, then `G505`..`G599`) - the program would run in the wrong frame or alarm.\n\n- New `frameWord` in the script maps the setup's word to the control's: `G54`..`G57` unchanged, `G58` -> `G505`, `G59` -> `G506`. A word naming no settable frame is refused by name (counted warning, blocks the post).\n- The probing result that sets an offset goes through the same mapping, so a probe asked to set offset 6 now writes `$P_UIFR[6,..]` and re-selects `G506` (it was refused before, since the script knew `G59` was no frame). An offset past six never reaches the post: the stream parser already refuses `FOUND SET` past G59.\n- The setup stays the one source of truth (`setup::wcs_slot`); only the word this post writes changes. No other post, no golden changes (no golden covered offsets 5/6 on this post).\n- Decision (write G505/G506 rather than refuse): `docs/decisions/934-sinumerik-g505.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests:\n- `sinumerik_work_offsets::sinumerik_posts_offsets_one_to_six_as_their_settable_frames` - posts sections on all six `WCS_SLOTS` words; asserts `G54 G55 G56 G57 G505 G506` in the opening blocks and no `G58`/`G59` word anywhere.\n- `sinumerik_work_offsets::sinumerik_refuses_a_work_offset_that_names_no_settable_frame`\n- `probe_dialects::sinumerik_sets_the_sixth_offset_as_frame_g506` (replaces `sinumerik_refuses_setting_g59_by_name`, whose behaviour this fix deliberately changes)\n\nGate: quick on head 26e8610e green - `app probe_dialects (1 fn)` ok, `app sinumerik_work_offsets (2 fn)` ok. Batch on the first commit (d9cd719c): geometry, tools, post, sim, motion suites and clippy -D warnings green; app suites failed only on a probe pin I then dropped (unreachable - the stream parser refuses a slot past G59 first); two failures not from this diff: ui `theme_files` (known main-side) and cl `headless_bin::cl_bin_prints_move_stats` (expects `arcs 30`, reads `arcs 33` on `contour_disc_hole.cl`; crates/cl is untouched here).\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNot run on a real 840D or a simulator. **This changes posted G-code, so it waits on a Hub run before it is flagged ready.** The posted word is pinned at the script seam (engine + `sinumerik.cps`), not through a full setup post with the Sinumerik machine selected.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\nfork synced at v0.17.0 (branched from upstream/main)\n\nChangelog: Siemens 840D post writes work offsets 5 and 6 as the settable frames G505 / G506 instead of G58 / G59 (programmable offsets on that control); a probe can now set offset 6\n\nFixes #934\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
